---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import EmbeddingCostCalculator from '../../components/EmbeddingCostCalculator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Embedding Cost Calculator"
  description="Estimate the cost of embedding your documents for a RAG or vector search pipeline across OpenAI, Voyage, Cohere, and Gemini."
>
  <EmbeddingCostCalculator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why embedding costs sneak up on you</h2>
  <p>
    Building a RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) system means embedding
    every document chunk before you can search over it. For large document
    sets, this one-time indexing cost can be bigger than expected —
    especially if you re-embed on every content update.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this calculator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Estimate how many chunks or documents you'll embed.</li>
    <li>Estimate the average token count per chunk (typically 200-800 tokens for RAG).</li>
    <li>Compare total indexing cost across embedding providers.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Embedding Cost FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Is this a recurring cost?</strong> No — embedding is typically a
    one-time cost per document, unless you update or re-chunk your content,
    in which case you'll re-embed the changed portions.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does chunk size affect cost?</strong> Yes — smaller chunks mean
    more total embeddings for the same document, which can increase total
    token usage due to overlap between chunks.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
